          "quote": "refractory-element-based superalloys, including Cr-based [ 4 – 6 ], Nb-based [ 7 , 8 ], W-based [ 9 , 10 ], Ti-based [ 11 , 12 ], and RCCAs [ 13 ].",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "068c9ba3cdd66c99:part:001"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "alloy_system_6",
      "name": "(MoTaTi)92-x-8Cr-Alx alloy",
      "material_category": null,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": "6",
          "section": null,
          "quote": "A recent study by Laube et al. [21] demonstrated that a pseudo-binary diagram (similar to Fig. 1b) for (MoTaTi)92-x-8Cr-Alx can be used to form B2 precipitates within a BCC matrix by tuning alloy composition, providing a strategy for achieving a B2-in-BCC microstructure in RCCAs.",
          "chunk_id": "068c9ba3cdd66c99:part:002"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "alloy_system_7",
